# Windows scripts MUST keep CRLF in the working tree.
#
# This repo's core.autocrlf is `input`: CRLF is stripped on commit and NOTHING is
# put back on checkout. So every .bat here lands on disk LF-only, and cmd.exe
# cannot resolve `goto` labels in an LF-only batch file — start.bat died with
# "cannot find the batch label specified - dbsync_done" the first time git
# re-checked it out. These rules make the checkout write CRLF, whatever autocrlf says.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
*.vbs text eol=crlf
